fix(auth): separate unauthenticated observation from confirmed bypass

checkUnauthenticated emitted CRITICAL "Missing authentication on endpoint" for
ANY 2xx returned without credentials, and graded its confidence off response
body length. scanner.Endpoint carried no auth-expectation field, so the check
structurally could not tell a public endpoint from a bypassed one: docs pages,
health checks and SPA routes each produced a CRITICAL that the decision layer
then blocked on.

The premise the claim needs — "authentication was expected here" — was never
supplied by anything, and a status code cannot supply it. The knowledge existed
and was discarded: python/analyzers/spec_parser.py already parses per-operation
and global `security`.

Now resolved in Go, where crawler.fromSpec already holds the parsed spec:

  models.AuthExpectation  unknown ("") | public | required
  Endpoint.AuthExpectation                 set by fromSpec
  Evidence.AuthExpectation{,Source}        carried to the decision layer

  required → "Authentication requirement bypassed", CRITICAL, and the
             contradiction counts as INDEPENDENT corroboration
  unknown  → "Unauthenticated endpoint observed", MEDIUM, never gates
  public   → INFO

Unknown is a real third state. Collapsing it into public would suppress real
bypasses; collapsing it into required is the bug being fixed. Evidence is
preserved in all three cases (Rule 3) — only the claim's strength changes, and
the evidence text now says WHY a finding is unconfirmed.

No path is hardcoded. TestClassificationIsSemanticNotPathBased probes the same
/status twice and asserts the claim differs only with the declared expectation.

specAllowsAnon mirrors spec_parser._allows_anon including the `security: [{}]`
form, where len([{}]) == 1 makes a naive truthiness check read an explicit
opt-out as a requirement.

ADJACENT DEFECT FIXED: correlator_v2 restores producer-set flags for
pass-through findings because the ProvenanceIndex is built AFTER correlation.
The AuthExpectation pair is the same shape as the four flags already listed
there, so it is restored alongside them — otherwise the new signal would work
on a pure-DAST scan and be silently dead on every --url + --code scan.

The two auth titles are now named constants. Fourteen test sites carried their
own copy of the literal, which is why changing the claim broke them all.

Full suite: 39 packages ok, 0 failures.

Refs RC-2.

